surtr-backend-nvidia talks to the NVIDIA Management Library (NVML).

NVML is NVIDIA's library. It is installed with the NVIDIA display driver
(nvml.dll on Windows, libnvidia-ml.so.1 on Linux) and is loaded from the
user's system at run time. Surtr does not include, redistribute or link
against any NVIDIA binary or header.

The function and type declarations in src/ffi.rs were written by hand from
NVIDIA's public NVML API documentation. They are part of Surtr and licensed
like the rest of the project (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

NVIDIA and NVML are trademarks of NVIDIA Corporation. Surtr is not affiliated
with or endorsed by NVIDIA.
